{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ETAiaPQH9h5vTBKdTUMj5b","type":"tool_result","content":"80\t# Unknown key -> no probe. The ledger's descriptive `local_probe` (if present)\n81\t# is intentionally NOT executed; it is human documentation only.\n82\t_PROBE_ARGV: Dict[str, List[str]] = {\n83\t    \"claude_code\": [\"claude\", \"--version\"],\n84\t    \"agent_sdk_ts\": [\n85\t        \"node\", \"-e\",\n86\t        \"console.log(require('@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk/package.json').version)\",\n87\t    ],\n88\t    \"agent_sdk_py\": [\n89\t        \"python3\", \"-c\",\n90\t        \"import importlib.metadata as m; print(m.version('claude-agent-sdk'))\",\n91\t    ],\n92\t    # PLAN-155 Wave 0 (debate A12): the Codex substrate is watched by TWO\n93\t    # ledger entries backed by the SAME read-only binary probe — `codex_cli`\n94\t    # (pair-rail reviewer flag-surface, PLAN-142 lineage; previously had no\n95\t    # probe registered) and `codex_harness` (Codex-as-HOST hooks/config/rules\n96\t    # schema surface, PLAN-155).\n97\t    \"codex_cli\": [\"codex\", \"--version\"],\n98\t    \"codex_harness\": [\"codex\", \"--version\"],\n99\t    # PLAN-178 W1.2-5c (codex S306 r5 P2 cure): the native per-agent usage\n100\t    # source is a shape OF the Claude Code harness — its installed version IS\n101\t    # the harness version, so a harness bump marks this component drifted and\n102\t    # triggers the promised native-shape re-fingerprint.\n103\t    \"cc_native_usage\": [\"claude\", \"--version\"],\n104\t}\n105\t\n106\t# Code-registered drift runbooks (PLAN-155 Wave 0, debate A12). Same posture\n107\t# as _PROBE_ARGV (Codex R2 P0): the ledger can only SELECT a component key —\n108\t# it can NEVER supply alert/procedure text of its own. When a component with\n109\t# a registered runbook drifts, the runbook is attached to that report row\n110\t# (`runbook`) and printed in text mode, so the alert names the exact\n111\t# re-record procedure instead of a bare version delta.\n112\t_CODEX_FIXTURE_RUNBOOK = (\n113\t    \"codex-cli drift — fixture re-record runbook (PLAN-155 debate A12): do \"\n114\t    \"NOT re-record fixtures against the new binary directly. (1) bump the \"\n115\t    \"pin FIRST via the ADR-182 pin ceremony (codex-cli-pin.txt semver range \"\n116\t    \"+ codex-cli-pin-manifest.json per-triple PAYLOAD sha256 — the retired \"\n117\t    \"codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt launcher hash is a tombstone); (2) THEN \"\n118\t    \"re-record the PLAN-155 Wave-1 \"\n119\t    \"host-adapter fixtures under .claude/hooks/tests/fixtures/adapters/codex/ \"\n120\t    \"(each fixture carries _meta.codex_cli_version; the pin-range test stays \"\n121\t    \"RED until fixtures are re-recorded or explicitly waived); (3) run the \"\n122\t    \"per-bump re-verification checklist in ADR-161 (hook envelope schema, \"\n123\t    \"PreToolUse interception surface, /hooks trust-hash keying, SubagentStart \"\n124\t    \"continue:false, Stop decision:block, execpolicy prefix_rule syntax).\"\n125\t)\n126\t_DRIFT_RUNBOOKS: Dict[str, str] = {\n127\t    \"codex_cli\": _CODEX_FIXTURE_RUNBOOK,\n128\t    \"codex_harness\": _CODEX_FIXTURE_RUNBOOK,\n129\t}\n130\t\n131\t\n132\tdef load_ledger(path: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n133\t    \"\"\"Read the substrate-watch ledger. None on any failure (fail-open).\"\"\"\n134\t    try:\n135\t        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n136\t            data = json.load(fh)\n137\t        if not isinstance(data, dict):\n138\t            return None\n139\t        return data\n140\t    except (OSError, ValueError):\n141\t        return None\n142\t\n143\t\n144\tdef _extract_version(text: str) -> Optional[str]:\n145\t    \"\"\"First semver-ish token in `text` (e.g. 'claude 1.2.3 (...)' -> '1.2.3').\"\"\"\n146\t    match = _VERSION_RE.search(text or \"\")\n147\t    return match.group(1) if match else None\n148\t\n149\t\n150\tdef _run_version_cmd(argv: List[str]) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:\n151\t    \"\"\"Execute a registered version probe (shell=False). Test seam — unit tests\n152\t    patch THIS symbol to script probe output without touching a real binary.\"\"\"\n153\t    return subprocess.run(  # nosec B603 — fixed argv from _PROBE_ARGV (code-defined, NOT ledger-controlled)\n154\t        argv,\n155\t        shell=False,\n156\t        capture_output=True,\n157\t        text=True,\n158\t        timeout=_PROBE_TIMEOUT_S,\n159\t    )\n160\t\n161\t\n162\tdef _probe_installed(key: str) -> Tuple[Optional[str], str]:\n163\t    \"\"\"Resolve the installed version for component ``key`` via its code-defined\n164\t    probe in ``_PROBE_ARGV``. Returns (version|None, note).\n165\t\n166\t    The command is NEVER taken from ledger data (Codex R2 P0) — only the key\n167\t    selects which hardcoded argv runs. Fail-soft: an unregistered key, missing\n168\t    binary, non-zero exit, timeout, or unparseable output all degrade to\n169\t    (None, <reason>) — never raises.\n170\t    \"\"\"\n171\t    argv = _PROBE_ARGV.get(key)\n172\t    if not argv:\n173\t        return None, \"no probe registered for component %r\" % key\n174\t    try:\n175\t        proc = _run_version_cmd(argv)\n176\t    except (subprocess.TimeoutExpired, OSError) as exc:\n177\t        return None, \"probe unavailable (%s)\" % type(exc).__name__\n178\t    if proc.returncode != 0:\n179\t        return None, \"probe exit %d (not installed?)\" % proc.returncode\n180\t    version = _extract_version((proc.stdout or \"\") + \" \" + (proc.stderr or \"\"))\n181\t    if version is None:\n182\t        return None, \"probe ran but no version token parsed\"\n183\t    return version, \"ok\"\n184\t\n185\t\n186\tdef build_report(\n187\t    ledger: Optional[Dict[str, Any]],\n188\t    *,\n189\t    probe_installed: bool = False,\n190\t) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n191\t    \"\"\"Pure-ish builder (the only impurity is the opt-in version probe).\n192\t\n193\t    Returns a dict with: status, summary, source_stale, components[].\n194\t    NEVER raises.\n195\t    \"\"\"\n196\t    if ledger is None:\n197\t        return {\n198\t            \"schema\": 1,\n199\t            \"fail_open\": True,\n200\t            \"status\": \"current\",\n201\t            \"summary\": \"substrate-watch ledger missing/corrupt — advisory, \"\n202\t            \"treated as no-drift (run from the repo root; the ledger ships at \"\n203\t            \".claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json)\",\n204\t            \"source_stale\": False,\n205\t            \"components\": [],\n206\t        }\n207\t\n208\t    meta = ledger.get(\"_meta\") if isinstance(ledger.get(\"_meta\"), dict) else {}\n209\t    source_stale = bool(meta.get(\"source_stale\", False))\n210\t    components_in = ledger.get(\"components\")\n211\t    components_in = components_in if isinstance(components_in, list) else []\n212\t\n213\t    rows: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n214\t    any_drift = False\n215\t    any_unknown = False\n216\t    for comp in components_in:\n217\t        if not isinstance(comp, dict):\n218\t            continue\n219\t        last_seen = comp.get(\"last_seen\") if isinstance(comp.get(\"last_seen\"), dict) else {}\n220\t        seen_version = str(last_seen.get(\"version\", \"unknown\"))\n221\t        row: Dict[str, Any] = {\n222\t            \"key\": comp.get(\"key\", \"?\"),\n223\t            \"label\": comp.get(\"label\", comp.get(\"key\", \"?\")),\n224\t            \"last_seen_version\": seen_version,\n225\t            \"last_seen_date\": str(last_seen.get(\"date\", \"unknown\")),\n226\t            \"installed_version\": None,\n227\t            \"probe_note\": \"not probed (--probe-installed off)\",\n228\t            \"drift\": False,\n229\t            \"runbook\": None,\n230\t        }\n231\t        if seen_version == \"unknown\":\n232\t            any_unknown = True\n233\t        if probe_installed:\n234\t            installed, note = _probe_installed(str(comp.get(\"key\", \"\")))\n235\t            row[\"installed_version\"] = installed\n236\t            row[\"probe_note\"] = note\n237\t            codex_current = (\n238\t                str(comp.get(\"key\", \"\")) in (\"codex_cli\", \"codex_harness\")\n239\t                and cli_currency.compare_semver(\n240\t                    installed, cli_currency.CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR\n241\t                ) is not None\n242\t                and cli_currency.compare_semver(\n243\t                    installed, cli_currency.CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR\n244\t                ) >= 0\n245\t            )\n246\t            if installed is not None and codex_current:\n247\t                row[\"currency\"] = \"compatible\"\n248\t            elif installed is not None and seen_version != \"unknown\" and installed != seen_version:\n249\t                row[\"drift\"] = True\n250\t                any_drift = True\n251\t                # Attach the code-registered runbook (None-safe): the alert\n252\t                # names the fixture re-record procedure, not just the delta.\n253\t                row[\"runbook\"] = _DRIFT_RUNBOOKS.get(str(comp.get(\"key\", \"\")))\n254\t        rows.append(row)\n255\t\n256\t    if source_stale or any_unknown:\n257\t        status = \"stale-ledger\"\n258\t        summary = (\n259\t            \"substrate-watch ledger never Owner-refreshed against the live \"\n260\t            \"changelog (source_stale or last_seen=unknown) — PENDING-OWNER: %s\"\n261\t            % str(meta.get(\"refresh_recipe\", \"run --refresh for the recipe\"))\n262\t        )\n263\t    elif any_drift:\n264\t        status = \"drift\"\n265\t        drifted = [r[\"key\"] for r in rows if r[\"drift\"]]\n266\t        summary = \"installed substrate differs from last-reconciled for: %s\" % drifted\n267\t    else:\n268\t        status = \"current\"\n269\t        summary = \"substrate reconciled — installed matches last_seen for all components\"\n270\t\n271\t    return {\n272\t        \"schema\": 1,\n273\t        \"fail_open\": False,\n274\t        \"status\": status,\n275\t        \"summary\": summary,\n276\t        \"source_stale\": source_stale,\n277\t        \"components\": rows,\n278\t    }\n279\t\n280\t\n281\t_REFRESH_RECIPE = \"\"\"\\\n282\tPENDING-OWNER substrate-watch refresh (no model tokens; one doc fetch each):\n283\t  For each component in .claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json:\n284\t    1. WebFetch the _meta.sources value for that key. A STRING is one\n285\t       URL; a LIST means fetch EACH URL in it (PLAN-155 A12: e.g.\n286\t       codex_harness = release feed + the three host-harness doc pages).\n287\t    2. Single-URL key: read the topmost version + release date on the\n288\t       page. LIST key: last_seen.version tracks the versioned feed (the\n289\t       first URL); the doc pages carry no version — record last_seen.date\n290\t       as the newest visible 'last updated' across ALL pages, and treat\n291\t       ANY observed change on a doc page as drift for that component\n292\t       EVEN IF the release feed shows no new version (docs-only schema\n293\t       drift is exactly the class this entry watches; on drift follow\n294\t       the component's registered runbook in _DRIFT_RUNBOOKS).\n295\t    3. Set components[key].last_seen.version + .date to those values.\n296\t    4. Set _meta.fetched to today and _meta.source_stale to false.\n297\t  This is Owner-run by design — the nightly agent stays no-network\n298\t  (ADR-136-AMEND-1). The fetch bills no model tokens; record nothing\n299\t  billable. After it lands, dimension vii reports 'current' until the\n300\t  next upstream release.\"\"\"\n301\t\n302\t\n303\tdef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n304\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n305\t        description=\"Claude Code + Agent-SDK substrate drift watch (PLAN-135 O12).\"\n306\t    )\n307\t    parser.add_argument(\n308\t        \"--ledger\", default=DEFAULT_LEDGER_PATH,\n309\t        help=\"path to substrate-watch.json (default: alongside this script)\","}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c629bb59-4a63-4b18-b933-a99f884e3507","uuid":"0a7c2e09-09a2-4141-9826-4500599434e9","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:22:26.883Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/.claude/scripts/check-substrate-watch.py","content":"# Unknown key -> no probe. The ledger's descriptive `local_probe` (if present)\n# is intentionally NOT executed; it is human documentation only.\n_PROBE_ARGV: Dict[str, List[str]] = {\n    \"claude_code\": [\"claude\", \"--version\"],\n    \"agent_sdk_ts\": [\n        \"node\", \"-e\",\n        \"console.log(require('@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk/package.json').version)\",\n    ],\n    \"agent_sdk_py\": [\n        \"python3\", \"-c\",\n        \"import importlib.metadata as m; print(m.version('claude-agent-sdk'))\",\n    ],\n    # PLAN-155 Wave 0 (debate A12): the Codex substrate is watched by TWO\n    # ledger entries backed by the SAME read-only binary probe — `codex_cli`\n    # (pair-rail reviewer flag-surface, PLAN-142 lineage; previously had no\n    # probe registered) and `codex_harness` (Codex-as-HOST hooks/config/rules\n    # schema surface, PLAN-155).\n    \"codex_cli\": [\"codex\", \"--version\"],\n    \"codex_harness\": [\"codex\", \"--version\"],\n    # PLAN-178 W1.2-5c (codex S306 r5 P2 cure): the native per-agent usage\n    # source is a shape OF the Claude Code harness — its installed version IS\n    # the harness version, so a harness bump marks this component drifted and\n    # triggers the promised native-shape re-fingerprint.\n    \"cc_native_usage\": [\"claude\", \"--version\"],\n}\n\n# Code-registered drift runbooks (PLAN-155 Wave 0, debate A12). Same posture\n# as _PROBE_ARGV (Codex R2 P0): the ledger can only SELECT a component key —\n# it can NEVER supply alert/procedure text of its own. When a component with\n# a registered runbook drifts, the runbook is attached to that report row\n# (`runbook`) and printed in text mode, so the alert names the exact\n# re-record procedure instead of a bare version delta.\n_CODEX_FIXTURE_RUNBOOK = (\n    \"codex-cli drift — fixture re-record runbook (PLAN-155 debate A12): do \"\n    \"NOT re-record fixtures against the new binary directly. (1) bump the \"\n    \"pin FIRST via the ADR-182 pin ceremony (codex-cli-pin.txt semver range \"\n    \"+ codex-cli-pin-manifest.json per-triple PAYLOAD sha256 — the retired \"\n    \"codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt launcher hash is a tombstone); (2) THEN \"\n    \"re-record the PLAN-155 Wave-1 \"\n    \"host-adapter fixtures under .claude/hooks/tests/fixtures/adapters/codex/ \"\n    \"(each fixture carries _meta.codex_cli_version; the pin-range test stays \"\n    \"RED until fixtures are re-recorded or explicitly waived); (3) run the \"\n    \"per-bump re-verification checklist in ADR-161 (hook envelope schema, \"\n    \"PreToolUse interception surface, /hooks trust-hash keying, SubagentStart \"\n    \"continue:false, Stop decision:block, execpolicy prefix_rule syntax).\"\n)\n_DRIFT_RUNBOOKS: Dict[str, str] = {\n    \"codex_cli\": _CODEX_FIXTURE_RUNBOOK,\n    \"codex_harness\": _CODEX_FIXTURE_RUNBOOK,\n}\n\n\ndef load_ledger(path: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Read the substrate-watch ledger. None on any failure (fail-open).\"\"\"\n    try:\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            data = json.load(fh)\n        if not isinstance(data, dict):\n            return None\n        return data\n    except (OSError, ValueError):\n        return None\n\n\ndef _extract_version(text: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"First semver-ish token in `text` (e.g. 'claude 1.2.3 (...)' -> '1.2.3').\"\"\"\n    match = _VERSION_RE.search(text or \"\")\n    return match.group(1) if match else None\n\n\ndef _run_version_cmd(argv: List[str]) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:\n    \"\"\"Execute a registered version probe (shell=False). Test seam — unit tests\n    patch THIS symbol to script probe output without touching a real binary.\"\"\"\n    return subprocess.run(  # nosec B603 — fixed argv from _PROBE_ARGV (code-defined, NOT ledger-controlled)\n        argv,\n        shell=False,\n        capture_output=True,\n        text=True,\n        timeout=_PROBE_TIMEOUT_S,\n    )\n\n\ndef _probe_installed(key: str) -> Tuple[Optional[str], str]:\n    \"\"\"Resolve the installed version for component ``key`` via its code-defined\n    probe in ``_PROBE_ARGV``. Returns (version|None, note).\n\n    The command is NEVER taken from ledger data (Codex R2 P0) — only the key\n    selects which hardcoded argv runs. Fail-soft: an unregistered key, missing\n    binary, non-zero exit, timeout, or unparseable output all degrade to\n    (None, <reason>) — never raises.\n    \"\"\"\n    argv = _PROBE_ARGV.get(key)\n    if not argv:\n        return None, \"no probe registered for component %r\" % key\n    try:\n        proc = _run_version_cmd(argv)\n    except (subprocess.TimeoutExpired, OSError) as exc:\n        return None, \"probe unavailable (%s)\" % type(exc).__name__\n    if proc.returncode != 0:\n        return None, \"probe exit %d (not installed?)\" % proc.returncode\n    version = _extract_version((proc.stdout or \"\") + \" \" + (proc.stderr or \"\"))\n    if version is None:\n        return None, \"probe ran but no version token parsed\"\n    return version, \"ok\"\n\n\ndef build_report(\n    ledger: Optional[Dict[str, Any]],\n    *,\n    probe_installed: bool = False,\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Pure-ish builder (the only impurity is the opt-in version probe).\n\n    Returns a dict with: status, summary, source_stale, components[].\n    NEVER raises.\n    \"\"\"\n    if ledger is None:\n        return {\n            \"schema\": 1,\n            \"fail_open\": True,\n            \"status\": \"current\",\n            \"summary\": \"substrate-watch ledger missing/corrupt — advisory, \"\n            \"treated as no-drift (run from the repo root; the ledger ships at \"\n            \".claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json)\",\n            \"source_stale\": False,\n            \"components\": [],\n        }\n\n    meta = ledger.get(\"_meta\") if isinstance(ledger.get(\"_meta\"), dict) else {}\n    source_stale = bool(meta.get(\"source_stale\", False))\n    components_in = ledger.get(\"components\")\n    components_in = components_in if isinstance(components_in, list) else []\n\n    rows: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n    any_drift = False\n    any_unknown = False\n    for comp in components_in:\n        if not isinstance(comp, dict):\n            continue\n        last_seen = comp.get(\"last_seen\") if isinstance(comp.get(\"last_seen\"), dict) else {}\n        seen_version = str(last_seen.get(\"version\", \"unknown\"))\n        row: Dict[str, Any] = {\n            \"key\": comp.get(\"key\", \"?\"),\n            \"label\": comp.get(\"label\", comp.get(\"key\", \"?\")),\n            \"last_seen_version\": seen_version,\n            \"last_seen_date\": str(last_seen.get(\"date\", \"unknown\")),\n            \"installed_version\": None,\n            \"probe_note\": \"not probed (--probe-installed off)\",\n            \"drift\": False,\n            \"runbook\": None,\n        }\n        if seen_version == \"unknown\":\n            any_unknown = True\n        if probe_installed:\n            installed, note = _probe_installed(str(comp.get(\"key\", \"\")))\n            row[\"installed_version\"] = installed\n            row[\"probe_note\"] = note\n            codex_current = (\n                str(comp.get(\"key\", \"\")) in (\"codex_cli\", \"codex_harness\")\n                and cli_currency.compare_semver(\n                    installed, cli_currency.CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR\n                ) is not None\n                and cli_currency.compare_semver(\n                    installed, cli_currency.CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR\n                ) >= 0\n            )\n            if installed is not None and codex_current:\n                row[\"currency\"] = \"compatible\"\n            elif installed is not None and seen_version != \"unknown\" and installed != seen_version:\n                row[\"drift\"] = True\n                any_drift = True\n                # Attach the code-registered runbook (None-safe): the alert\n                # names the fixture re-record procedure, not just the delta.\n                row[\"runbook\"] = _DRIFT_RUNBOOKS.get(str(comp.get(\"key\", \"\")))\n        rows.append(row)\n\n    if source_stale or any_unknown:\n        status = \"stale-ledger\"\n        summary = (\n            \"substrate-watch ledger never Owner-refreshed against the live \"\n            \"changelog (source_stale or last_seen=unknown) — PENDING-OWNER: %s\"\n            % str(meta.get(\"refresh_recipe\", \"run --refresh for the recipe\"))\n        )\n    elif any_drift:\n        status = \"drift\"\n        drifted = [r[\"key\"] for r in rows if r[\"drift\"]]\n        summary = \"installed substrate differs from last-reconciled for: %s\" % drifted\n    else:\n        status = \"current\"\n        summary = \"substrate reconciled — installed matches last_seen for all components\"\n\n    return {\n        \"schema\": 1,\n        \"fail_open\": False,\n        \"status\": status,\n        \"summary\": summary,\n        \"source_stale\": source_stale,\n        \"components\": rows,\n    }\n\n\n_REFRESH_RECIPE = \"\"\"\\\nPENDING-OWNER substrate-watch refresh (no model tokens; one doc fetch each):\n  For each component in .claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json:\n    1. WebFetch the _meta.sources value for that key. A STRING is one\n       URL; a LIST means fetch EACH URL in it (PLAN-155 A12: e.g.\n       codex_harness = release feed + the three host-harness doc pages).\n    2. Single-URL key: read the topmost version + release date on the\n       page. LIST key: last_seen.version tracks the versioned feed (the\n       first URL); the doc pages carry no version — record last_seen.date\n       as the newest visible 'last updated' across ALL pages, and treat\n       ANY observed change on a doc page as drift for that component\n       EVEN IF the release feed shows no new version (docs-only schema\n       drift is exactly the class this entry watches; on drift follow\n       the component's registered runbook in _DRIFT_RUNBOOKS).\n    3. Set components[key].last_seen.version + .date to those values.\n    4. Set _meta.fetched to today and _meta.source_stale to false.\n  This is Owner-run by design — the nightly agent stays no-network\n  (ADR-136-AMEND-1). The fetch bills no model tokens; record nothing\n  billable. After it lands, dimension vii reports 'current' until the\n  next upstream release.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Claude Code + Agent-SDK substrate drift watch (PLAN-135 O12).\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--ledger\", default=DEFAULT_LEDGER_PATH,\n        help=\"path to substrate-watch.json (default: alongside this script)\",","numLines":230,"startLine":80,"totalLines":359}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ETAiaPQH9h5vTBKdTUMj5b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
